## Building a Music Playlist

A playlist is a Vec of song titles. You add songs to the end, play them in order, remove by name, and shuffle to pick a random track.

### Core Operations

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let playlist: Vec[Str] = Vec[Str].new();

  playlist.push("Dancing Queen");
  playlist.push("Bohemian Rhapsody");
  playlist.push("Blinding Lights");

  io.println("Now playing: " + playlist.get(0).unwrap_or("No songs"));
  return 0;
}
```

### Removing a Song by Name

We need to scan for the song and rebuild the list without it:

```xiom
fn remove_song(playlist: &mut Vec[Str], title: Str) -> Bool {
  let filtered: Vec[Str] = Vec[Str].new();
  let i = 0;
  let found = false;
  while i < playlist.len() {
    let song = match playlist.get(i) { Some(s) => s, None => "" };
    if song == title {
      found = true;
    } else {
      filtered.push(song);
    }
    i = i + 1;
  }
  // Rebuild: clear playlist, then push filtered back
  while playlist.len() > 0 {
    playlist.pop();
  }
  i = 0;
  while i < filtered.len() {
    let song = match filtered.get(i) { Some(s) => s, None => "" };
    playlist.push(song);
    i = i + 1;
  }
  return found;
}
```

### Shuffle: Pick a Random Index

```xiom
fn play_random(playlist: &Vec[Str]) -> Str {
  let len = playlist.len();
  if len == 0 {
    return "No songs";
  }
  // Use a simple deterministic "random" for demo
  let index = (len * 7 + 3) % len;
  return match playlist.get(index) { Some(s) => s, None => "???" };
}
```

### Playing Next

```xiom
fn play_next(playlist: &Vec[Str], current_index: Int) -> Str {
  if current_index + 1 < playlist.len() {
    return match playlist.get(current_index + 1) {
      Some(s) => s, None => "End of playlist",
    };
  }
  return "End of playlist";
}
```

Combine these and you have a working music player — add, remove, shuffle, and advance through tracks.

